{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60012","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89597","text":"stackdocs — specification"}]},{"id":"blk-60013","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89598","text":"What this system is, what it must do, what it must never do, and how to tell a correct implementation from a wrong one. Derived from the code at "},{"id":"spn-89599","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-89600","text":" in the ProjectAmp2 monorepo."}]},{"id":"blk-60014","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89601","text":"1. Purpose"}]},{"id":"blk-60015","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89602","text":"stackdocs produces a single self-contained HTML file ("},{"id":"spn-89603","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/index.html"},{"id":"spn-89604","text":") and a machine-readable sidecar ("},{"id":"spn-89605","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-89606","text":") that together mirror every documentation markdown file across the [&] monorepo as a navigable site. The site's routes are the source paths; an agent or a human can map between the two without a lookup table."}]},{"id":"blk-60016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89607","text":"The build also produces one BendScript document per source file ("},{"id":"spn-89608","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/bend/*.bend.json"},{"id":"spn-89609","text":"), each validated and content-addressed."}]},{"id":"blk-60017","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89610","text":"2. Invariants"}]},{"id":"blk-60018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89611","text":"These properties must hold on every successful build. A build that violates any of them must fail, not degrade."}]},{"id":"blk-60019","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89612","text":"2.1 Route-source identity"}]},{"id":"blk-60020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89613","text":"For every page, "},{"id":"spn-89614","marks":["code"],"text":"route === source path"},{"id":"spn-89615","text":". The build must not move, rename, or re-root any file. A reader seeing route "},{"id":"spn-89616","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-89617","text":" must be able to open that exact path on disk."}]},{"id":"blk-60021","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89618","text":"2.2 BendScript validity"}]},{"id":"blk-60022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89619","text":"Every page must be a valid BendScript document per the "},{"id":"spn-89620","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-89621","text":" schema. A document that cannot be validated degrades to a raw code-block view but is still validated in that form — it is never omitted."}]},{"id":"blk-60023","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89622","text":"2.3 Content-address fixpoint"}]},{"id":"blk-60024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89623","text":"Every page is content-addressed (CIDv1). The round-trip "},{"id":"spn-89624","marks":["code"],"text":"parse(serialize(parse(doc)))"},{"id":"spn-89625","text":" must produce the same CID. This is checked across the entire corpus; a single violation fails the "},{"id":"spn-89626","marks":["code"],"text":"fixpointAll"},{"id":"spn-89627","text":" flag in the build report."}]},{"id":"blk-60025","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89628","text":"2.4 Build provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-60026","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89629","text":"Every build embeds a git commit hash as both a "},{"id":"spn-89630","marks":["code"],"text":"<meta name=\"build-commit\">"},{"id":"spn-89631","text":" tag and a field in the model JSON. The commit is derived from the latest non-"},{"id":"spn-89632","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89633","text":" commit ("},{"id":"spn-89634","marks":["code"],"text":"git log -1 --format=%H -- . \":(exclude)dist\""},{"id":"spn-89635","text":"), not from HEAD. This is the \"two-commit chain\" strategy: source changes are committed first (the "},{"id":"spn-89636","marks":["italic"],"text":"source commit"},{"id":"spn-89637","text":"), then "},{"id":"spn-89638","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89639","text":" is rebuilt and committed on top (the "},{"id":"spn-89640","marks":["italic"],"text":"artifact commit"},{"id":"spn-89641","text":"). The provenance always points to the source commit, breaking the self-referential cycle where committing "},{"id":"spn-89642","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89643","text":" would change HEAD, which would change the embedded hash, which would require another commit."}]},{"id":"blk-60027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89644","text":"If no source commit can be resolved to a 40-hex-char SHA, the build fails. The build date is derived from the source commit's timestamp, not the wall clock, so that repeated builds of the same source commit produce byte-identical output regardless of when the artifact commit is made."}]},{"id":"blk-60028","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89645","text":"2.5 Derived facts, not literals"}]},{"id":"blk-60029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89646","text":"Canonical numbers (versions, law counts, trial counts) are read at build time from the file that owns them — "},{"id":"spn-89647","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-89648","text":" for npm versions, "},{"id":"spn-89649","marks":["code"],"text":"mix.exs"},{"id":"spn-89650","text":" for Elixir versions, the conformance harness source for law counts. A missing or unreadable source is a hard build failure. No fallback to a stale literal exists. The mechanism lives in "},{"id":"spn-89651","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89652","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-60030","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89653","text":"2.6 Cross-doc link integrity"}]},{"id":"blk-60031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89654","text":"Relative "},{"id":"spn-89655","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-89656","text":" links within the corpus that resolve to a known route become internal navigation edges. Unresolvable links degrade gracefully (they render as-is) but do not fail the build. The curated build ("},{"id":"spn-89657","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89658","text":") is stricter: a broken internal edge is a hard failure."}]},{"id":"blk-60032","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89659","text":"3. The dark factory"}]},{"id":"blk-60033","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89660","text":"The build derives a four-phase status model called the \"dark factory\" from "},{"id":"spn-89661","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-89662","text":". The four phases, in fixed order, are:"}]},{"id":"blk-60034","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60036","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89663","marks":["bold"],"text":"perceive"},{"id":"spn-89664","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60035","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60038","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89665","marks":["bold"],"text":"decide"},{"id":"spn-89666","text":" — an explicit GAP (no step in §4 owns a decision-phase evidence rung)"}]}],"id":"blk-60037","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60040","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89667","marks":["bold"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-89668","text":" — sourced from §4 step 1"}]}],"id":"blk-60039","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60042","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89669","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure"},{"id":"spn-89670","text":" — sourced from §4 step 7"}]}],"id":"blk-60041","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60043","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89671","text":"Each sourced phase carries an evidence-ladder rung parsed from the owning table row. The valid rungs are: "},{"id":"spn-89672","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-89673","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89674","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-89675","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89676","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-89677","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89678","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89679","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89680","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-89681","text":". A phase with no owning source is recorded as a named GAP with an explanatory string, not fabricated."}]},{"id":"blk-60044","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89682","text":"3.1 Dark-factory constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-60045","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60047","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89683","text":"The phase count must be exactly four, in the order above."}]}],"id":"blk-60046","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60049","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89684","text":"A GAP must not carry a rung or a source field."}]}],"id":"blk-60048","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60051","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89685","text":"The presentation layer ("},{"id":"spn-89686","marks":["code"],"text":"home.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89687","text":") must not contain any hard-coded evidence-rung literals ("},{"id":"spn-89688","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-89689","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89690","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-89691","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89692","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89693","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89694","marks":["code"],"text":"external"},{"id":"spn-89695","text":"). The word "},{"id":"spn-89696","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-89697","text":" is allowed because it collides with the ship-status vocabulary; the unambiguous rung literals are the test boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-60050","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60053","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89698","text":"These constraints are enforced by "},{"id":"spn-89699","marks":["code"],"text":"test-dark-factory.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89700","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89701","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-89702","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-60052","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60054","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89703","text":"4. The verification gate"}]},{"id":"blk-60055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89704","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-deployed.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89705","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89706","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run verify:deployed"},{"id":"spn-89707","text":") is the gate for the docs reporting claim to reach "},{"id":"spn-89708","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-89709","text":". It:"}]},{"id":"blk-60056","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60058","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89710","text":"Fetches the production site at "},{"id":"spn-89711","marks":["code"],"text":"https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com"},{"id":"spn-89712","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60057","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60060","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89713","text":"Extracts the embedded commit hash and model JSON."}]}],"id":"blk-60059","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89714","text":"Verifies internal consistency (meta tag commit === model commit)."}]}],"id":"blk-60061","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60064","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89715","text":"Checks that the local source commit (latest non-"},{"id":"spn-89716","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89717","text":" commit) matches the production commit. Under the two-commit chain, this is the commit that produced the build, not HEAD."}]}],"id":"blk-60063","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89718","text":"Rebuilds locally from the same source."}]}],"id":"blk-60065","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89719","text":"Compares the dark-factory model field-by-field: phase order, rungs, sources, GAP status and text."}]}],"id":"blk-60067","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89720","text":"Checks that the production HTML contains visible references to "},{"id":"spn-89721","marks":["code"],"text":"darkFactory"},{"id":"spn-89722","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89723","marks":["code"],"text":"GAP"},{"id":"spn-89724","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-89725","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-89726","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60069","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89727","text":"Fails if any divergence is found, including commit parity."}]}],"id":"blk-60071","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89728","text":"The script does not deploy. It only asserts that what is deployed matches what the source produces."}]},{"id":"blk-60074","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89729","text":"5. Deployment"}]},{"id":"blk-60075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89730","text":"Deployment is a manual "},{"id":"spn-89731","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-docs.sh"},{"id":"spn-89732","text":" invocation that:"}]},{"id":"blk-60076","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89733","text":"Rebuilds the atlas from the live monorepo."}]}],"id":"blk-60077","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89734","text":"Clones the deploy repo ("},{"id":"spn-89735","marks":["code"],"text":"c-u-l8er/docs"},{"id":"spn-89736","text":") into a temp directory."}]}],"id":"blk-60079","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60082","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89737","text":"Mirrors "},{"id":"spn-89738","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89739","text":" into the clone."}]}],"id":"blk-60081","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89740","text":"Commits and pushes only if something changed."}]}],"id":"blk-60083","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60085","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89741","text":"Cloudflare Pages serves the deploy repo's "},{"id":"spn-89742","marks":["code"],"text":"dist/"},{"id":"spn-89743","text":" verbatim with no build step. The deploy repo is not this repo — it is a separate git repository that receives pre-built artifacts."}]},{"id":"blk-60086","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89744","text":"6. Two build modes"}]},{"id":"blk-60087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89745","text":"The codebase has two build pipelines:"}]},{"id":"blk-60088","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60090","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89746","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build-atlas.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-89747","text":" (primary, "},{"id":"spn-89748","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build"},{"id":"spn-89749","text":") — filesystem-mirror mode. Scans the entire monorepo, ingests every "},{"id":"spn-89750","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-89751","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89752","marks":["code"],"text":"prompts/"},{"id":"spn-89753","text":" markdown file. Produces the homepage theme system (Runefort bands), the dark-factory model, and the atlas sidecar. This is what ships."}]}],"id":"blk-60089","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89754","marks":["bold"],"text":"`build.mjs`"},{"id":"spn-89755","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-89756","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run build:curated"},{"id":"spn-89757","text":") — curated mode. A hand-authored 21-page proof-of-concept defined entirely in "},{"id":"spn-89758","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89759","text":". Stricter link checking (broken internal edge = build failure). Supports transclusion ("},{"id":"spn-89760","marks":["code"],"text":"{{key}}"},{"id":"spn-89761","text":"). Does not scan the filesystem. Does not produce "},{"id":"spn-89762","marks":["code"],"text":"atlas.json"},{"id":"spn-89763","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-60091","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89764","text":"The reason for keeping both is not recorded in the code. The curated build appears to be the earlier prototype; the atlas build superseded it for production use."}]},{"id":"blk-60094","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89765","text":"7. Must-never-do"}]},{"id":"blk-60095","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89766","text":"Must never move, rename, or reorganize source files. The mirror property is load-bearing."}]}],"id":"blk-60096","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89767","text":"Must never hard-code a fact (version, count) that has a canonical source file. The derivation in "},{"id":"spn-89768","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89769","text":" is the only path."}]}],"id":"blk-60098","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89770","text":"Must never hard-code evidence-rung literals in the presentation layer."}]}],"id":"blk-60100","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89771","text":"Must never produce a deployment without a resolvable commit hash."}]}],"id":"blk-60102","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89772","text":"Must never silently succeed when a canonical source is missing or unreadable."}]}],"id":"blk-60104","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89773","text":"Must never fabricate a dark-factory rung or source for a phase that has no owning step."}]}],"id":"blk-60106","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60108","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89774","text":"8. Dependencies"}]},{"id":"blk-60109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89775","text":"Two runtime dependencies, both from the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-60110","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89776","marks":["code"],"text":"@bendscript/core"},{"id":"spn-89777","text":" 0.1.0-alpha.0 — validation, content-addressing, serialization, parsing."}]}],"id":"blk-60111","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89778","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-89779","text":" 0.10.0 — imported by "},{"id":"spn-89780","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89781","text":" path traversal (law counting), not used as a runtime governance kernel in this codebase."}]}],"id":"blk-60113","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89782","text":"No other runtime dependencies. The build runs on Node.js with only built-in modules beyond these two."}]},{"id":"blk-60116","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89783","text":"9. Open questions"}]},{"id":"blk-60117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89784","text":"These are decisions the code makes whose reasons are not recorded:"}]},{"id":"blk-60118","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89785","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why keep the curated build?"},{"id":"spn-89786","text":" "},{"id":"spn-89787","marks":["code"],"text":"build.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89788","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-89789","marks":["code"],"text":"content.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89790","text":" are a complete second pipeline with hand-authored content. The atlas build superseded it for production. Whether the curated build is still exercised, depended on, or slated for removal is not stated."}]}],"id":"blk-60119","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89791","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why does `box-and-box` appear in `package.json`?"},{"id":"spn-89792","text":" It is listed as a dependency but "},{"id":"spn-89793","marks":["code"],"text":"sources.mjs"},{"id":"spn-89794","text":" reads from the monorepo path "},{"id":"spn-89795","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/"},{"id":"spn-89796","text":", not from "},{"id":"spn-89797","marks":["code"],"text":"node_modules"},{"id":"spn-89798","text":". The installed package may be unused. The reason for its inclusion is not recorded."}]}],"id":"blk-60121","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89799","marks":["bold"],"text":"Fallback-vs-failure asymmetry."},{"id":"spn-89800","text":" The atlas build treats an unparseable document as a graceful fallback (raw code block); the curated build treats a broken internal edge as a hard failure. Both are defensible but the difference in failure philosophy is not explained."}]}],"id":"blk-60123","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60125","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-89801","text":"10. What is already written down elsewhere"}]},{"id":"blk-60126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89802","text":"The referenced ADR documents ("},{"id":"spn-89803","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0004"},{"id":"spn-89804","text":" through "},{"id":"spn-89805","marks":["code"],"text":"ADR-0008"},{"id":"spn-89806","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89807","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPERVISOR.md"},{"id":"spn-89808","text":", "},{"id":"spn-89809","marks":["code"],"text":"workbench spec"},{"id":"spn-89810","text":") are about WebHost.Systems and the workbench, not about this codebase. They share vocabulary (deployment immutability, provenance, telemetry) but do not describe stackdocs. The "},{"id":"spn-89811","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"},{"id":"spn-89812","text":" in this directory is the closest thing to a prior spec; this document supersedes it for normative purposes."}]},{"id":"blk-60127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-89813","text":"No design document for this codebase existed before this file."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraw7bsw2klildjsiy2esn45aw2sfnkijs5le5t3ak7st37dc435v2a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}